---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Polaroid from '../components/Polaroid.astro';
import { elsewhere } from '../lib/site';
import photo from '../assets/tj.jpg';
---

<Base title="About" active="about" crumb={[{ label: 'about' }]}>
  <article>
    <p>
      Hey,{' '}
      <a
        class="jeff"
        href="https://youtu.be/QVX3THmhSsw?t=90"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        my name is Jeff
      </a>{' '}
      :)
    </p>
    <p>
      I'm a software engineer. Lately most of my time goes into AI, mostly poking at local models to
      see when they're the right tool for the job. I build my own harnesses to test them and try new
      ways of putting them to work. I think a lot of software is going to be rebuilt around AI over
      the next few years, and I want to help with that. And there's always a fun side project or two
      going :)
    </p>
    <Polaroid
      src={photo}
      alt="Jeff sitting on an orange couch on a rooftop at night, city lights behind him"
      note="oh hey, that's me btw"
    />
    <p>
      This blog is where I think out loud. I wanted somewhere to show how I think, and somewhere I
      can come back to in a few years to see how that thinking changed.
    </p>
    <p>
      The look comes from the exercise books we took notes in back in school, and from Diary of a
      Wimpy Kid, which was my favourite book back then lol.
    </p>
    <h2>elsewhere</h2>
    <p>
      {elsewhere.map((link, i) => (
        <>
          {i > 0 && ' · '}
          <a href={link.href}>{link.label}</a>
        </>
      ))}
    </p>
    <p class="meta updated">last updated 2026-10-26</p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  /* "my name is Jeff" reads as plain text with a dotted underline */
  .jeff {
    color: inherit;
    border-bottom: 1.5px dotted var(--ink);
  }

  .jeff:hover {
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .updated {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }
</style>
